<title>BELGIUM: Belgian unions call day of action ahead of 1997 budget.</title>
<headline>Belgian unions call day of action ahead of 1997 budget.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1996-09-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Belgium's two main public sector unions on Tuesday called for a day of action over reports pension cuts will be announced in the 1997 budget next week.</p>
<p>In a statement, the unions called on members to support a rally in the centre of the capital Brussels on Thursday. Belga news agency reported that provincial rallies were also planned.</p>
<p>Belgian RTBF radio said Prime Minister Jean-Luc Dehaene would break from the government's budget preparations to meet union leaders on Wednesday.</p>
<p>The budget is due to be presented to parliament on October 1.</p>
</text>
